      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Speaker"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Impact printers (e.g., Dot Matrix) physically strike the ribbon on paper, whereas Non-Impact printers (e.g., Laser, Inkjet) use non-contact methods.",
        "Plotters are specifically tested as the preferred output device for Computer-Aided Design (CAD) and high-quality vector blueprints.",
        "Distinguish clearly between softcopy output (Monitors, Speakers) and hardcopy output (Printers, Plotters)."
      ],
      "id": "88ez4qb"
